## Coding Conventions

Coding conventions for this project live in `docs/coding-conventions.md`.
Any agent writing or reviewing code in this project MUST read that file
before starting. This applies whether the work is inside the AI/DLC
pipeline or a one-off change. All work in this repository, pipeline or
not, follows the minimum-mechanism principle (KISS): the smallest
design that meets the requirement, no speculative machinery,
simplification valued equally with addition. Details:
`docs/coding-conventions.md`.

---

## Tool-Output Routing (context-mode)

context-mode injects its own routing guidance (sandbox for processing;
native Bash/Read for mutations, short observations, and to-Edit files).
Two AI/DLC-specific rules it cannot know:

- **Routing is a nudge, not a Rule-18 mandate.** "Prefer sandbox" never
  gates or blocks work — sometimes the native tool IS correct.
- **Gate evidence stays command-reproducible.** The durable artifact is the
  raw output on disk plus the command that produced it (`… | tee
  test-results/<name>.txt`), never a model summary — the reviewer re-runs
  and byte-matches. context-mode only changes how you derive the summary.

